From ebfa1f486cf4b8e15b40aa2c777d9ab77564b1b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jev-router <jev-router@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:48:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): add gemini-4-argon to gemini-web with
 live-calibrated mode selection (#16573)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Argon is a real, selectable mode on Pro accounts (live menu: "4 Argon /
Complex tasks") but was not advertised for gemini-web — the upstream PR is
[defer], so requests for it died with unknown_model before ever reaching the
UI. Adds the model to the gemini-web registry and the mode-selection map.

The mode-selection selectors were UNVALIDATED guesses (they failed live:
gemini-3.7-flash could never confirm its switch). Recalibrated against a live
signed-in session (2026-10-16):
- the picker is button[aria-label^="Open mode picker"] opening a gem-menu of
  gem-menu-item[role="menuitem"] entries
- item matching is regex on visible text, version-agnostic (the menu now
  advertises 3.8 Flash / 3.5 Flash-Lite while the gweb ids remain
  gemini-3.7-flash / gemini-3.1-flash-lite; the Flash pattern excludes
  Flash-Lite explicitly)
- read-back polls the picker's aria-label attribute until it confirms

Also makes the selection flow stale-handle-proof: Angular detaches the picker
button between query and click (elementHandle.click: Element is not attached
to the DOM -> 500), so the toggle click re-queries and retries, and the
indicator is re-queried each poll. All fail-closed paths (#13381) unchanged:
no confirmation -> 400 unsupported_control_for_provider.

Live smoke on a signed-in session: Argon mode switch confirmed (picker ->
menu -> Argon -> aria-label verified -> prompt submitted). Full generation
currently stalls Google-side under automation throttling (PENDING-RESPONSE
never resolves) — same throttle that affects the other gweb models here, not
specific to this change.

Tests: 15 mode-selection tests (incl. argon confirmed/missing-item/mismatch),
26 gemini-web unit tests, all gemini-web suites green; typecheck:core clean.
